  "scope": "Actual original-form dimension-bounded detecting families on every original symmetric twisted H1 subspace. Global finiteness is derived by restricting coefficient scalars on the same cocycles, and the native finite-family theorem constructs joint injectivity. All preceding arithmetic and symmetric conclusions remain for the same residual witness.",
  "sourceAssemblyReview": "The final source theorem unpacks the preceding actual original regular-prime consumer, keeps the same residual witness and all conclusions, and proves a bounded jointly detecting family on every actual original H1 subspace. Finiteness comes from an injection of the same cocycles under prime-field scalar restriction, not an assumed cohomology comparison. Native dimension induction is reused. Failed monolithic elaboration attempts and unexecuted drafts are retained; proof limits remain unchanged."
